.\" robodr-firewall-gw(8). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-firewall-gw/src/bin/robodr-firewall-gw.rs, the crate README
.\" (crates/robodr-firewall-gw/README.md), the units in packaging/systemd/
.\" and docs/OPERATIONS.md section 6.6. Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-FIREWALL\-GW 8 "2026-10-31" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-firewall\-gw \- RoboDR in\-path Motion Firewall gateway: decide every motion datagram that crosses a bridge (NFQUEUE)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-firewall\-gw run \-\-config
.I FILE
.br
.B robodr\-firewall\-gw check\-config \-\-config
.I FILE
.br
.B robodr\-firewall\-gw ruleset \-\-config
.I FILE
.br
.B robodr\-firewall\-gw webrtc\-block \-\-peer
.I IPV4
.RB [ \-\-flow
.IR PEER_PORT , ROBOT_IP , ROBOT_PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout\-s
.IR 1..86400 ]
.br
.B robodr\-firewall\-gw
.RB ( \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robodr\-firewall\-gw
runs on a sensor box that bridges the robot controller's network port and
the robot's. A netfilter ruleset (rendered by the
.B ruleset
command) hands every UDP datagram entering from the controller side on the
DDS port ranges and the configured legacy ports to an NFQUEUE. For each one
the gateway decodes the motion command (Unitree SDK2 RTPS
.BR LowCmd_ ,
sport / loco / arm requests, arm SDK, hands, ROS 2
.B /cmd_vel
and joint trajectories, Go1 legacy UDP), asks the Motion Firewall
(robodr\-firewall) for a verdict against the locked profile's envelope and
the firewall configuration, and accepts the datagram unchanged, rewrites it
in place (a limited value, a hold of the last accepted frame, a removed
sample) or drops it. It never originates traffic and opens no IP socket.
.PP
It is
.B not a safety\-rated device.
It is a cyber\-security control in front of the robot's own safety
functions (e\-stop, safety controller, motor drivers' protections), which
remain primary. It can only pass, reduce, hold or remove commands that
cross the bridge.
.PP
While the gateway is not running the kernel applies the ruleset's
.BR queue.on_gateway_down :
.B fail_closed
(default) drops the queued motion datagrams;
.B bypass
lets them pass unchecked (refused for humanoid joint channels).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Load and check the configuration, the profile (with its trust checks) and
the firewall configuration, bind the NFQUEUE and decide until
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR SIGINT .
Notifies systemd
.RB ( READY=1 ,
.B WATCHDOG=1
every
.BR housekeeping_ms ,
.BR STOPPING=1 ).
Needs
.B CAP_NET_ADMIN
only.
.TP
.B check\-config
Everything
.B run
checks before binding the queue, without touching the network:
configuration, profile and its trust checks, in
.B enforce
mode the firewall file's signature, firewall compile, channel / codec /
slot count / profile
.B motion_types
agreement, the humanoid / bypass rule. Prints a one\-line summary.
.TP
.B ruleset
Print the idempotent POSIX
.BR sh (1)
setup script for this configuration: bridge netfilter sysctls; an nft
.B bridge
table that bridges only IPv4 and ARP from the controller port (and
single\-tagged IPv4 / ARP of the VLANs in
.BR queue.vlan_ids );
untracked traffic with IPv4 defragmentation before the queue; the
.B ROBODR_GW
chain that drops fragments and queues the DDS and legacy ports; the
.B ROBODR_GW_OBS
chain that copies the robot side's UDP to NFLOG; the WebRTC section when
configured.
.B robodr\-firewall\-gw\-rules.service
runs it at boot. The rules are meant to stay when the gateway stops.
.TP
.B webrtc\-block
Print the
.BR nft (8)
command that adds a Go2 WebRTC peer (or one flow of it) to the
.B blocked_peers
.RB ( blocked_flows )
set of the ruleset's
.B bridge robodr_gw_rtc
table for
.B \-\-timeout\-s
seconds (default 600). Run the printed command as root.
.SH CONFIGURATION
A JSON file (unknown keys refused), by default
.IR /etc/robodr/firewall\-gw.json ;
examples in
.IR /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/ .
The main keys:
.TP
.B mode
.B enforce
(requires a locked, trusted profile and a signed firewall file) or
.B observe
(decide and record what enforcement would have done; forward everything
unchanged).
.TP
.BR profile ", " profile_trust
The locked model profile and its trust settings (as agentd's
.B sensor.profile_trust ;
the anti\-rollback state is read, never written).
.TP
.B firewall
The Motion Firewall configuration (channels, joint channels, platform). In
.B enforce
mode
.IB firewall .sig
must exist: a signature by the key that signed the profile, over the
profile's digest and the file's bytes, written by
.BR "robodr\-commission sign\-firewall" .
An unsigned, edited, or re\-paired file refuses the start (exit 2).
.TP
.B queue
.BR num ,
.BR max_len ,
.BR on_gateway_down ,
.BR controller_port ,
.BR robot_port ,
.BR vlan_ids .
.TP
.B rtps
Domain ids, extra port ranges, the malformed\-datagram and unknown\-writer
policies, the writer tables and the persisted writer
.BR state_file .
.TP
.B channels
One entry per enforced channel: the firewall channel, the codec, source
allowlists (IP, MAC), and the codec's own keys
.RB ( allowed_api_ids
is required for the sport,
.B obstacles_avoid
and
.B uwbswitch
request codecs,
.B allowed_high_modes
for
.BR go1_high_cmd ).
.TP
.BR max_queue_delay_ns ", " overload_interval_ms ", " overload_high_late
A datagram read later than
.B max_queue_delay_ns
(default 5 ms) gets the firewall's fault verdict; such late datagrams are
reported as one
.B robot.gateway.overload
finding per interval at most.
.TP
.BR events_path ", " status_path ", " findings_socket ", " restriction_path
The deviations file, the status / counters file, agentd's
.B gateway_feed
socket, and the
.B restrict_motion
restriction file written by
.BR robodr\-executor (8).
.PP
The complete reference is the crate README, section "Configuration".
.SH FINDINGS AND RECORDS
With
.BR findings_socket ,
the gateway's own findings
.RB ( robot.gateway.* ,
aggregated per housekeeping period), the Motion Firewall's deviations
.RB ( robot.firewall.* )
and decision summaries
.RB ( robodr\-gateway\-summary/v1 :
mode, fail behaviour, the digests of the configuration, firewall and
profile files, decision counters; at start, every 60 s and at a clean
stop) go to
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
which turns the findings into findings of its pipeline and appends the
summaries to its signed black box. The feed is written from its own
thread; the decision path never waits for it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/firewall\-gw.json
Configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/firewall\-gw/
State directory of the unit (status file, events file, writer state file).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/robodr\-firewall\-gw.service
The gateway
.RB ( Type=notify ,
user
.BR robodr\-gw ,
.B CAP_NET_ADMIN
only, FIFO priority 40, watchdog 2 s).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/robodr\-firewall\-gw\-rules.service
Oneshot that renders and applies the ruleset at boot, before
.BR network\-pre.target .
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
stop the gateway cleanly (final housekeeping, stop summary). There is no
reload signal: a changed configuration, profile or firewall file takes
effect at the next start, and a changed queue, port or VLAN setting needs
the ruleset re\-applied
.RB ( "systemctl restart robodr\-firewall\-gw\-rules robodr\-firewall\-gw" ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean stop, or the command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (NFQUEUE, signals).
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error, including a profile that fails its trust
checks or an unsigned firewall file in
.B enforce
mode (the unit does not restart on it).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
.BR robodr\-executor (8),
.BR robodr\-commission (1),
.BR nft (8),
.BR iptables (8),
.BR systemd.service (5)
.PP
